# Hello World

## Problem Title & Summary
Display the message `Hello World!` in the terminal.

## Logic & Approach
The program passes a string to Python's built-in `print()` function. The
function writes the message to standard output and ends the line.

## Time & Space Complexity
Time Complexity: O(1)
Space Complexity: O(1)

## Example Input & Output
```text
Input: None

Hello World!
```

## Run
Run with Python 3:
```text
python hello_world.py
```

## Flow Diagram
```text
Start
  |
  v
Call print("Hello World!")
  |
  v
Display message
  |
  v
End
```
